Here is the relationship as I understand it:

Work Order
has many Hole Details
each Hole Detail has 2 Hole Calculations
one Hole Calculation has product 000002 = Structural
one Hole Calculation has product 000001 = Finish

Each Hole Calculation also has a Volume field.

Then you have another table, which I understand as Work Order Product, where for each Work Order you keep a rolled-up total by product type:

one Work Order Product row for Structural
one Work Order Product row for Finish

And the value on each Work Order Product row should be:

Structural total = sum of all Hole Calculation volumes for that Work Order where vgsd_product = 000002
Finish total = sum of all Hole Calculation volumes for that Work Order where vgsd_product = 000001

So in plain words:

For a given Work Order, you want to aggregate all related Hole Calculation volumes by product type, and update the corresponding Work Order Product records with those totals.
